SUMMARY:Andrew Scotchie & Friends
DESCRIPTION:We’re SO excited to have Andrew Scotchie performing in the brewery again! It’s seriously awesome to b able to host this friend and local legend! \nJoin singer-songwriter Andrew Scotchie as he brings in a singer-songwriter showcase on one Monday every month.\nBorn and raised in Asheville\, Andrew Scotchie is everything rock-n-roll was meant to be: sweaty\, soul-stirring\, a little dangerous\, and absolutely alive. With the fire of the Stones\, the blues of Lightnin’ Hopkins\, and the message of a punk-fueled preacher\, Scotchie and his all-star band have become a staple of the Southeast music scene .\nHe’s shared stages with legends\, crowd-surfed dive bars\, and continues to craft his unique sound. His latest record\, Love Is Enough\, is a love letter to connection\, chaos\, and keeping your heart open in a world gone sideways.\n​\nThrough consistent heartfelt releases\, year round touring and active charity work\, Asheville N.C. native Andrew Scotchie is a celebrated creative force. His unique brand of rock n roll\, blues and Americana has an unmatched sense of urgency and unifying social commentary.\nFree show | All Ages | Food and Drink Available. \nFrench Broad River Brewery is more than just a place to enjoy a drink—it’s a community hub where great beer\, delicious pizza\, live music\, and good times come together. Just minutes from the Biltmore Estate & Downtown\, our taproom is a gathering spot for locals and visitors alike. We regularly host live music and entertainment in our taproom\, making French Broad River Brewery a lively hub of local activity. From bluegrass to reggae\, there’s always something happening. Check out our Events Page to see what’s coming up next!
URL:https://livemusicasheville.com/calendar/andrew-scotchie/2026-05-25/
LOCATION:French Broad River Brewery\, 101 Fairview Rd\, Asheville\, NC\, United States
CATEGORIES:Asheville Area,Live Music
ATTACH;FMTTYPE=image/jpeg:https://livemusicasheville.com/wp-content/uploads/2025/11/693022046_1564539842340013_6196656817889016594_n-e1778682202402.jpg
GEO:35.5662722;-82.5374054
